summary:
  A wake-up stops raising its standing order, so the retry switch can silence it.

history:
  An alarm hands the later death of its station to the heal road — the
  bundled chime only guards the first 25 seconds, and a stream that played
  and then died is explicitly the heal road's case. Both refusals the retry
  switch owns therefore exempt the alarm, and the exemption is only as real
  as the flag it reads. Drop the flag and an alarm set for 7:00 goes quiet at
  7:10 with the sleeper still asleep, on a setting about ordinary listening
  that nobody would connect to their alarm.

target:
  package/contents/ui/AlarmEngine.qml

find:
          app._wantsPlaying = true;
          _alarmStandingOrder = true;

replace:
          app._wantsPlaying = true;
          _alarmStandingOrder = false;

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_invariants.py::test_a_wake_up_keeps_its_road_back_whatever_the_switch_says.
  Also by tests/qml/tst_alarmengine.qml::test_a_firing_alarm_outlives_a_spent_retry_budget,
  which fires a real alarm and feeds its own flag to the real decision.
  Line-neutral.
